      "settings": {
        "eyebrow_text": "The problem it solves",
        "heading": "<p>Start line is hard to trust. LINE ONE makes it clear.</p>",
        "copy": "<p>If you’ve ever thought you read it right and still missed left or right, this is often why. LINE ONE helps you see whether the ball started on your aim — then build a quieter stroke that holds the line.</p>",
        "ritual_heading": "A simple 5-minute drill",
        "note": "Go slow. You’re training start line, not pace contests.",
        "panel_eyebrow": "Quick read",
        "panel_title": "Own the first foot of the putt.",
        "panel_copy": "Think of every putt as a start, then a roll. If the start is offline, the rest never mattered. Get the first foot right, then add distance.",
